OL,3,AMore than 170,000 respiratory cases
OL,4,Arecorded in haze-choked Indonesia
OL,5,
OL,6,FSome 175,000 people in Indonesia have
OL,7,Fsuffered from respiratory illness since
OL,8,FAugust, its health ministry said, as it
OL,9,Fcontinues to battle wildfires that have
OL,10,Fraged for weeks.
OL,12,FMore than 40,000 cases ` which range
OL,13,Ffrom coughs to bronchitis and more
OL,14,Fserious conditions like pneumonia `
OL,15,Finvolve toddlers.
OL,17,FForest fires have blanketed parts of
OL,18,Fthe country as well as neighbouring
OL,19,FMalaysia and Singapore in toxic smog,
OL,20,Fpushing air quality indices into
OL,21,F"unhealthy" territory.
OL,23,APub: 23-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,317,300,200,140,0,100
